agent-ops task task-093d4659-dc67-4144-b65c-f7b6d05167ba: Escape lesson library: integrate run branches and harden reflect
intent: Merge agent-ops/run-4257f3b203e34a6d-6b4dd0ce and -9d865b40 (keep both sides in lessons.ts and lesson-checks.mjs), set the escape runner test count to the integrated total, validate record.escapeOf/record.fix as full SHAs in reflect.ts, add --end-of-options in commitChange, and add an escape-reflect-ref-safe check. Docs, managed rules and the backfill follow as separate tasks.
criteria:
- lesson-library-integrated: Escape lessons work end to end: lesson files are parsed strictly and fail closed; a fired lesson left unanswered stops the surface gate with LESSON_MISSING and answers reach both reviewers; lesson fire/answer metrics are logged; escapes reflect writes one lesson / no-entry / not-run record per task with one retry on a rejected answer and refuses ineligible labels; finish refuses a scenario/requirement/review escape without a lesson file; the escapes report lists per-lesson counts; task create and the criteria advisory show path-matched lessons; and the escape-regression runner reports every rule and lesson check exactly once.
- reflect-ref-safe: escapes reflect refuses an escape record whose escapeOf or fix is not a full commit SHA (for example a value shaped like a git option) with ESCAPE_ORIGIN_INVALID before any git command runs, so git writes no file and the reflector is never called.
- agreed-design: The integrated code follows the agreed design choices that no check pins: the reflector is data-only and runs on the independent-review role's first target with no new role; lessons live in .agent-ops-escapes/lessons/<id>.json while the escape record format is unchanged; there is no per-task cap on fired lessons and nothing retires a lesson automatically.
